  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0005-p00005",
      "source_en": "I climbed a towering ridge, a height of ten thousand fathoms. The brambles tore my clothing to rags. I looked out beyond the cloud-dim sky— God, I could not see you. I dug into the hard shell of the earth, shattered the old lairs of the snake-drakes, and in the bottomless deep pool I cried out— God, I cannot hear you. I saw a child by the roadside; lively, beautiful, in ragged clothes; He cried, “Mother!”— love shining in his eyes. God, you are in his eyes! Composed on November 2, 1928.",
